You seem confused.<p>malice
&#x2F;măl′ĭs&#x2F;
noun<p>1. A desire to harm others or to see others suffer; extreme ill will or spite.<p>2. The intent to commit an unlawful act without justification or excuse.<p>3. An improper motive for an action, such as desire to cause injury to another.<p>None of the above apply to me. I don&#x27;t want to harm or injure anyone, and I don&#x27;t want anyone to suffer. Consumers choose suffering and choose to voluntarily accept harm and injury, and I wish they wouldn&#x27;t.<p>But you can&#x27;t force people to not harm themselves, it&#x27;s something they have to choose for themselves. Anyone who&#x27;s ever lived with or loved an alcoholic or drug addict understands this. The contempt isn&#x27;t for the person, it&#x27;s for the theft of the person&#x27;s faculties. The response to the person being unwilling to change is frustration with their choices, not contempt for the human being.
